.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
# Every .env variant, not just `.env` itself. A bare `.env` rule leaves `.env.cloud`,
# `.env.local-backup` and friends committable, which is exactly the file someone
# creates while switching between a local and a hosted database. `.env.example` is
# re-admitted below because it is deliberately tracked and holds no real values.
.env*
!.env.example
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Frontend build artifacts (continuity/api/app.py serves web/dist/ once built) --
# already matched by the unanchored node_modules/ and dist/ patterns above; listed
# explicitly too so they are unmistakable.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Generated data. ground_truth.json is regenerated deterministically from a seed and
# is deliberately kept out of the repo: the agent must never be able to read it.
data/*.json
data/*.parquet
data/*.csv
data/*.log
data/*.err

# This machine's GLOBAL ignore (~/.config/git/ignore) contains `**/docs/`, which silently
# excluded this project's entire docs tree from the repo: the design spec, ADR-001, all
# four sub-project plans, SETUP.md, the screenshots and the submission copy. CLAUDE.md is
# tracked and points at three of those paths, so a fresh clone contained references to
# files it did not have, and no setup instructions at all.
#
# Re-including needs the DIRECTORY negated first -- git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so `!docs/**` alone would do nothing.
!docs/
!docs/**

# Demo recordings: regenerate with docs/submission/record-demo.mjs. Listed AFTER the
# docs negation above, because later rules win and it would otherwise be re-included.
*.webm
*.mp4
docs/submission/*.webm
docs/submission/*.mp4
